# ErgoWorks Consulting — Open Questions

These questions gate implementation of the ErgoWorks Consulting campaign plan. Campaign **700072710** bidding is already resolved and is not an open question: it uses **Maximize Conversions with no target CPA**, as a standard non-portfolio strategy.

| Priority | Question | Why it matters | What it blocks |
|---|---|---|---|
| Critical | **Is Meta’s minimum A$600 per 30 days added on top of the existing Search budget, or reallocated from it?** | Search has a mature approximately A$40,000 trailing-12-month history and an observed A$3.0k–A$4.7k monthly range. Reallocation reduces proven demand capture; incremental funding produces a cleaner Meta baseline. | Final choice between Scenario 1 at A$4,246 and preferred Scenario 2 at A$4,846 per 30 days |
| Critical | **Can PMax receive at least A$50/day—A$1,500 per 30-day planning period—without destabilising Search?** | A 5–10% test slice at the current run-rate does not meet the required floor. PMax must be funded properly or parked. | Scenario 3, PMax relaunch planning and the final channel allocation |
| Critical | **GO/NO-GO: Does the client approve the free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot as the launch-default offer and dominant CTA, with the adjacent “preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis” caveat in every placement?** | The offer and caveat govern all baseline Search, Meta and landing-page variants. | Campaign copy, creative, form and landing-page launch |
| Critical | **GO/NO-GO: Does the client approve the complete ErgoStart → ErgoScale / ErgoCoach → ErgoControl offer ladder, including the eligibility and caveats in the canonical offer registry?** | The ladder names and packages are proposed, not yet approved commercial products. | Offer naming, routing, creative and sales handoff |
| Critical | **What exact Snapshot fulfilment promise is approved: consultant owner, eligibility, weekly capacity, 15-minute format, written three-point-summary template, turnaround, booking flow and response SLA?** | Copy must promise only what operations can consistently deliver. | Final Snapshot wording, availability, pacing and follow-up workflow |
| Critical | **What exact service geography is approved for the Snapshot and each paid offer, including remote versus onsite limits?** | “Australia-wide” and location-specific messaging cannot be published without confirmed coverage — and the live evidence has sharpened this into a **launch blocker**: the live site commits to **Sydney and Melbourne only**, while the 2026-07-12 search-terms pull spans Canberra, Sydney, Brisbane and national/"near me" terms. The only converting geo-specific term is "ergonomic office fyshwick" (A$250 / 18 clicks / 3 conv at 26% CTR); the Sydney/Melbourne/Brisbane/near-me geo terms appear in the pull but did not convert (`research/live-evidence-2026-07-12.md`). The LP cannot claim broader coverage than the live site until verified; if coverage IS Sydney/Melbourne-only, the Canberra spend needs a geo decision (keep, geo-modify or exclude), not just copy. | Geo targeting, exclusions, landing-page copy, the Appendix A geo-dynamic Canberra treatment, the Appendix B Canberra candidate ad group and lead routing |
| Critical | **What does ErgoWorks actually issue after training: an accredited certificate, a statement of attainment, participant attendance records, participant training-completion records, or another output?** | Certificate/course buyer type is UNCLASSIFIED, and programme action-status records are not participant credentials. Accreditation and participant-record claims require direct evidence and client sign-off. | Certificate Search test, certificate LP block and FAQ, organisational qualification, final ad copy and publication |
| Critical | **Are care-sector, online and refresher services actually supported; if so, in what onsite/remote format and approved service geography?** | Keyword demand verifies interest, not delivery capability. The live aged-care/disability/healthcare negatives also conflict with the proposed care build. | Care/online/refresher LP modules, care-sector negative reconciliation, geo labels and targeting, Search creative and publication |
| Critical | **GO/NO-GO: What exact qualified-call rule does the client approve, including minimum connected duration, operating-hours treatment, disposition criteria and exclusions?** | The native proxy remains Secondary; the deduplicated qualified import is the only Primary call signal. | Call tracking, CRM disposition, offline import and bidding |
| Critical | **Do we have admin access to the correct Meta Business Manager, ad account and Dataset/Pixel, plus authority to verify `ergoworksconsulting.com.au` and configure domain verification/AEM?** | Ownership and access are required before an isolated Meta build can be verified or launched. | Meta setup, Pixel/CAPI, domain verification, AEM and launch QA |
| Critical | **What are average contract value, contribution/delivery margin, qualified-lead-to-won rate and acceptable payback?** | These determine an affordable CAC, target CPQL and real target CPA. Raw revenue alone is insufficient. | Commercial target CPA, 3× Kill Rule, budget scaling, tCPA/tROAS assessment and ROI planning |
| Critical | **Which CRM is in use, and can it store click IDs, consent records, lead stages and values?** | Google and Meta need reliable offline quality signals so optimisation can move from raw forms toward qualified leads, proposals and won work. | Offline conversion imports, Google Data Manager, Meta CAPI feedback, CPQL reporting and closed-loop attribution |
| Critical | **What level of separation is approved for Consulting versus Physiotherapy?** Options include campaign-specific goals within the existing Ads account, a dedicated GA4 data stream/property, separate GTM scope, and a separate Meta Pixel/Dataset. | Google Ads account 9258098368 mixes Consulting and Physiotherapy. Health-adjacent data increases privacy and optimisation risk. Separation must not damage the Physiotherapy campaign through account-wide controls. | Conversion cleanup, audience creation, GTM/GA4 architecture, Meta launch, remarketing and reliable reporting |
| High | **Should paid remarketing receive a separate viable budget after audience creation, or remain parked?** | Remarketing should not share or dilute PMax’s floor. Its value depends on isolated audience size, privacy approval, frequency control and incremental contribution. | Display/Meta retargeting activation, creative volume and audience architecture |
| High | **How many free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshots can ErgoWorks deliver each week, and who owns response and follow-up?** The Snapshot is preliminary guidance only—**not a compliance assessment, medical assessment, diagnosis or certification**. | Meta may generate uneven lead flow. Slow response or insufficient delivery capacity would damage prospect experience and make channel results difficult to interpret. | Meta pacing, form scheduling, service-area limits, follow-up SLA and scale decisions |
| High | **Which proof assets are substantiated and approved in writing for paid-media use?** Specifically: reviews and rating, client logos, awards, Danone, and “ASX 100” claims. | These items remain **client sign-off required** and cannot be treated as usable evidence until their accuracy, wording and permissions are confirmed. | Final ad copy, landing-page proof sections, creative production and approval |
| High | **Is Joel the landing-page developer, what is the delivery window, and where will the page be hosted?** | The dedicated page is a dependency for message match, form design, consent controls, event tracking and paid-traffic routing. | Build schedule, technical specification, launch date, QA ownership and Search/Meta destination mapping |
| Medium | **What route or future subdomain should host the private shareable campaign page?** | A stable location is needed for client review and future handoff without mixing the Consulting project with ErgoEquip, Biosymm or unrelated site routes. | Shareable-page implementation, access model, URL mapping and future maintenance |

